# Real configs hold a live IP and (optionally) the client's private key
# inline — never commit these. Commit *.example.json instead.
server-config.json
client-config.json

# The server's real list of who's allowed to connect (names + public
# keys — not secret by themselves, but personal/deployment-specific,
# same reasoning as the configs above). Commit authorized_keys.example.json
# instead. Any *.key file holding a raw private key printed by
# cmd/genkey, if saved to disk instead of pasted into a config.
authorized_keys.json
*.key

# Throwaway dev certs (regenerated via `go run ./cmd/gencert`, or baked
# fresh into the Docker image).
devcerts/

# Trust-on-first-use pin files (pin_file config field) — not secret (just
# a public cert fingerprint), but local, machine-generated state, same
# reason ssh's known_hosts isn't checked into a repo either.
*.pin

# Build output
*.exe
tunprobe.exe
portprobe-linux

# cmd/tray's runtime log (see its own -config/tray.log, next to the exe
# — this repo-root one only shows up if someone runs it from here).
tray.log

# Reference-project scratch folders (other people's codebases dropped
# here for study, not part of this project) and the running notes taken
# on them — local-only, never pushed.
slorc/
owenlivkit/
IDEAS.md
